# Line endings must be pinned, not left to core.autocrlf.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and deployed to
# Linux containers. That combination silently rewrote every shell script to
# CRLF on checkout, and the backup sidecar then failed on its very first line:
#
#   /scripts/backup.sh: set: line 26: illegal option -
#
# "set -eu" had become "set -eu\r", so the carriage return was parsed as an
# option and the script exited before writing a single backup. The container
# stayed "Up" the whole time, so this failed completely silently.
#
# These rules make the working tree authoritative on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf

# Generated by tooling; never commit line-ending conversions for these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
